OL,3,ASpecial agents' blood and urine test
OL,4,Aresults stolen in FBI hack
OL,5,
OL,6,FCyber-criminals who hacked the FBI say
OL,7,Fthey have extremely sensitive medical
OL,8,Fdata for thousands of its special
OL,9,Fagents.
OL,11,FBBC News has seen samples of the stolen
OL,12,F"fitness-for-work" medical
OL,13,Fexaminations, which contain information
OL,14,Fsuch as blood and urine test results,
OL,15,Fand doctors' notes mentioning
OL,16,Fconditions such as a "shellfish and
OL,17,Fbanana allergy".
OL,19,FThe records include agents' full names
OL,20,Fand addresses, as well as references to
OL,21,Fmedical concerns including 'blood in
OL,22,Fthe urine' and 'high cholesterol'.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790416089
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ASpecial agents' blood and urine test
OL,4,Aresults stolen in FBI hack
OL,5,
OL,6,FExperts say the hack - which the FBI is
OL,7,Finvestigating - could leave agents
OL,8,Fvulnerable to scams, blackmail and
OL,9,Ftargeted attacks, as well as help
OL,10,Fcriminals impersonate law enforcement
OL,11,Fofficers.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
